# PR #332 Review

## Scope
- Reviewed diff from "'`gh pr diff 332`
- Reviewed PR metadata from `gh pr view 332 --json title,body,files`
- No `Task: @...` trailer found in PR body, so this is a pure code review (AC trailer checks skipped per instructions)

## Findings

### MUST-FIX
1. Unvalidated `--limit` can disable bounds entirely
- File: `src/cli/commands/session.ts:1920`
- `const limit = options.limit ? parseInt(options.limit, 10) : 50;` forwards unvalidated values to `searchSessionEvents`.
- With `--limit abc`, `parseInt` yields `NaN`; in `searchSessionEvents`, conditions like `totalMatches >= limit` are always false for `NaN`, so match limiting is effectively disabled.
- Impact: command may scan/return far more data than intended, violating the “maximum matches” contract.
- Fix: validate `--limit` as a positive integer and fail with `USAGE_ERROR` (or clamp/default consistently).

### SHOULD-FIX
1. Add defense-in-depth limit validation in store layer
- File: `src/sessions/store.ts:1220`
- `searchSessionEvents` trusts `options.limit` directly.
- If called outside CLI with invalid values, same unbounded behavior can recur.
- Fix: normalize to a safe positive integer in the store function as well.

## Posted Review
- Attempted to post `REQUEST_CHANGES` payload first.
- GitHub API returned HTTP 422: cannot request changes on your own pull request from this account.
- Posted equivalent review as `COMMENT` with inline comment instead.
- Review URL: https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/332#pullrequestreview-3766774403
